WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.486
Every air app gives you a number.

00:00:02.486 --> 00:00:09.148
But a number doesn't know who lives in your house — or how they cook, commute, or walk to school.

00:00:09.588 --> 00:00:10.635
AirMitra does.

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:13.027
A household air coach for India.

00:00:13.027 --> 00:00:19.980
Bhopal's headline is the median of its stations — with the range, distance and age beside it.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.977
Home is not always where you are.

00:00:22.977 --> 00:00:24.062
Set home once.

00:00:24.062 --> 00:00:27.393
Switch current from the header, or tap GPS.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:32.972
The badge says which one you're reading — and home is never overwritten.

00:00:33.412 --> 00:00:35.447
Choose your language first.

00:00:35.447 --> 00:00:40.948
Thirteen Indian languages — the interface, brief and every answer follow.

00:00:41.388 --> 00:00:46.918
Then the household: a father with asthma, an LPG kitchen, a school run.

00:00:46.918 --> 00:00:52.526
Gemini turns the reading into one directive, the reason, and a fallback.

00:00:52.526 --> 00:00:54.084
It refreshes hourly.

00:00:54.524 --> 00:00:55.483
Or just ask.

00:00:55.483 --> 00:01:03.152
'Is it safe for my father to walk now?' The answer uses the live air, his asthma and my routine.

00:01:03.152 --> 00:01:05.708
Gemini never invents the number.

00:01:06.148 --> 00:01:13.324
One tap builds a high-quality story card: best hours, three actions, the impact and one way to give back.

00:01:13.764 --> 00:01:16.613
No accounts, no analytics, no ads.

00:01:16.613 --> 00:01:19.377
The profile stays on your device.

00:01:19.377 --> 00:01:24.237
AirMitra — because clean air advice should know your home.

00:01:24.237 --> 00:01:27.588
Live at airmitra-app dot vercel dot app.
